<div id="recipe-82238-equipment" class="wprm-recipe-equipment-container wprm-block-text-normal" data-recipe="82238"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-equipment-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Equipment</h3><ul class="wprm-recipe-equipment wprm-recipe-equipment-list"><li class="wprm-recipe-equipment-item" style="list-style-type: disc;"><div class="wprm-recipe-equipment-name"><a href="https://amzn.to/45kad27" class="wprm-recipe-equipment-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow">1-inch Thick Metal Skewers</a></div></li></ul></div>
<div id="recipe-82238-ingredients" class="wprm-recipe-ingredients-container wprm-recipe-ingredients-no-images wprm-recipe-82238-ingredients-container wprm-block-text-normal wprm-ingredient-style-regular wprm-recipe-images-before" data-recipe="82238" data-servings="6"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-ingredients-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Ingredients</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-group"><h4 class="wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-bold">For the kebab</h4><ul class="wprm-recipe-ingredients"><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="1"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">2</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">red peppers</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded">red fresno chilis or &frac12; red bell pepper</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="2"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">2</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">lbs</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">ground lamb</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded">or 1 lb ground lamb + 1 lb ground beef</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="3"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">2</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">teaspoons</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">paprika</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="4"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">1</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">teaspoon</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name"><a href="https://amzn.to/4o5lZVn" class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow">Urfa chili flakes</a></span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded">or Aleppo pepper or red pepper flakes</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="5"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">1</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">tablespoon</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">kosher salt</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="6"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">1</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">teaspoon</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">black pepper</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="7"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">Water</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded">to wet your hands</span></li></ul></div><div class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-group"><h4 class="wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-bold">For the Sumac Onions</h4><ul class="wprm-recipe-ingredients"><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="9"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">1</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">medium-sized</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">red onion</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded">sliced</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="10"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">1</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">tablespoons</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">olive oil</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="11"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">2</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">tablespoons</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">lemon juice</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="12"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">&frac12;</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">teaspoon</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">Kosher salt</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="13"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">1</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">tablespoons</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">sumac</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="14"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">&frac14;</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">teaspoon</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name"><a href="https://amzn.to/4o5lZVn" class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow">Urfa chili flakes</a></span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded">Aleppo pepper or red pepper flakes</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="15"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">2</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">tablespoons</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">fresh parsley</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded">chopped</span></li></ul></div><div class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-group"><h4 class="wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-bold">To Serve with</h4><ul class="wprm-recipe-ingredients"><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="16"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">6</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">Lavash or pita bread</span></li></ul></div></div>
<div id="recipe-82238-instructions" class="wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-82238-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal" data-recipe="82238"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Instructions</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-group"><ul class="wprm-recipe-instructions"><li id="wprm-recipe-82238-step-0-0" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Start by preparing the peppers. Remove the seeds and chop them as finely as you can. Place the chopped peppers in a colander set over a bowl and let them drain to release their juices. Once drained, transfer them to a large mixing bowl.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-82238-step-0-1" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Add the ground lamb, paprika, Aleppo pepper, salt, and black pepper to the bowl with the peppers.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Lamb-Adana-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="Ground lamb mixed with red peppers and spices in a bowl." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Lamb-Adana-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Lamb-Adana-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Lamb-Adana-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Lamb-Adana-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Lamb-Adana.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Lamb-Adana.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-82238-step-0-2" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Using clean hands, mix everything together until fully combined and the seasonings are evenly distributed.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-82238-step-0-3" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Divide the meat mixture evenly based on the number of skewers you have. For example, if you have 3 skewers, divide the mixture into 3 equal portions.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Adana-seasoning-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="A person is threading the meat onto the skewer." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Adana-seasoning-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Adana-seasoning-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Adana-seasoning-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Adana-seasoning-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Adana-seasoning.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Adana-seasoning.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-82238-step-0-4" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Take one portion, shape it into a ball, and gently insert the skewer through the center.</span></div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-82238-step-0-5" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Fill a small bowl with cold tap water and keep it nearby. Using your hands, carefully press and spread the meat down the length of the skewer, turning it as you go to ensure even thickness all around. Lightly wet your fingers as needed to prevent the meat from sticking to your hands. Remember that just a little water is enough to help shape the kebabs without making the mixture too wet.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Adana-kebap-recipe-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="Adana kebab on skewers ready to grill." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Adana-kebap-recipe-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Adana-kebap-recipe-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Adana-kebap-recipe-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Adana-kebap-recipe-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Adana-kebap-recipe.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Adana-kebap-recipe.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-82238-step-0-6" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Once shaped, gently press and secure the top and bottom edges of the meat where it starts and ends on the skewer. This is an essential step in that it helps prevent the meat from breaking apart during grilling.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-82238-step-0-7" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">To create the traditional ridges, use your thumb and forefinger to lightly press along the length of the kebab, making shallow marks every couple of inches. Rotate the skewer and repeat on the other side. These ridges help the meat cook evenly and give the kebabs their signature look.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-82238-step-0-8" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Preheat your gas grill to 400&deg;F-425&deg;F. Clean the grill grates well and brush them with oil to prevent sticking.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Ground-lamb-kebabs-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="Turkish Adana on the grill." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Ground-lamb-kebabs-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Ground-lamb-kebabs-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Ground-lamb-kebabs-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Ground-lamb-kebabs-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Ground-lamb-kebabs.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Ground-lamb-kebabs.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-82238-step-0-9" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Once the grill is ready, place the Adana kebab skewers on the grates. Grill for 10-12 minutes, turning them often so they cook evenly and develop a nice char on the outside.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-82238-step-0-10" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Keep in mind that because the meat has a higher fat content, you may experience flare-ups. Stay close to the grill and adjust the heat as needed to prevent burning.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-82238-step-0-11" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Once cooked to your liking, cover the meat with foil and let it rest for 5-10 minutes.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-82238-step-0-12" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">While the meat is resting, make the sumac onions. In a medium-sized bowl, mix the sliced onions, olive oil, lemon juice, salt, sumac, and red pepper flakes.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Turkish-lamb-kebabs-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="Sumac onions in a bowl." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Turkish-lamb-kebabs-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Turkish-lamb-kebabs-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Turkish-lamb-kebabs-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Turkish-lamb-kebabs-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Turkish-lamb-kebabs.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Turkish-lamb-kebabs.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-82238-step-0-13" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Using clean hands, gently massage the onion mixture until slightly softened. Garnish with parsley.</span></div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-82238-step-0-14" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">When ready to assemble your Adana kebab, grab a lavash (or pita bread), place the meat on top, and garnish with sumac onions. Roll and serve right away.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Turkish-Adana-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="Adana kebab served on lavash with sumac onions on top." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Turkish-Adana-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Turkish-Adana-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Turkish-Adana-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Turkish-Adana-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Turkish-Adana.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Turkish-Adana.jpg"></div> </li></ul></div></div>
